# Task 8B2 report — pure V5 feedback-round runtime

## Outcome

Created `core/pit_optimizer_v5/runtime.py` and added only its minimal package exports. The module is a
pure dependency-injected state machine; it contains no filesystem, Git, Docker, subprocess, provider
gateway, CLI, replay, or market-data implementation.

## Implemented boundary

- Frozen input/result/failure, deadline, candidate-evidence, materialization, lease, and projection
  values plus narrow runtime Protocols.
- Exact Task 8B1 role recovery: the request is reconstructed and persisted before use;
  `FreshPersistedRoleRequestV5` is the only value accepted by `invoke_once`, while an existing request
  can only load a complete matching role event/package or go through `reconcile_once`. The terminal
  package and `role_completion` event are durable before its artifact is consumed.
- Authenticated projection and parent selection precede investigator, controller-owned novelty,
  author, deterministic rendering, validation/probes, quick selection, rotated discovery episodes,
  one complete critic batch, final records, archive reduction/checkpoint, and owned cleanup.
- Persisted rendered, quick, episode, role, lease, cleanup, and terminal outcome events are reused on
  restart. Completed quick/episode/role work is not repeated.
- Exact/source and suite-local behavioral duplicates remain untestable; only manifest-capped,
  behaviorally distinct quick survivors receive all four discovery episodes and all evaluator
  scenarios. Campaign CAGR is recomputed through the Task 6 authority.
- Failed terminal critic attempts create `critic_unavailable` with the full typed pre-critic evidence
  identity batch, no experiment records, and no checkpoint/archive mutation. No-novel and novelty
  exhaustion likewise create only their Task 8A durable terminal authorities.
- Final records are accepted only from the injected factory after one accepted critic artifact. All
  records are create-only before the archive reducer runs, and the checkpoint is published before
  cleanup. A checkpointed restart schedules cleanup only.
- Stage deadlines use the exact manifest values and monotonic time, cancellation is checked at stage
  boundaries, dependency exceptions are reduced to stable codes, and cleanup receives only recovered
  or newly issued opaque handles whose campaign/round ownership is exact.

Concrete workspace/worker/evaluator/provider/CLI composition remains deliberately deferred to Task
8C/9.

## Direct verification

A temporary deterministic in-memory fake harness (removed after use) produced:

- `V5_RUNTIME_HAPPY_SMOKE_OK`: exact investigator → author → critic sequence, two final records
  (`evaluated`, `quick_rejected`), one archive entry, checkpoint, then cleanup.
- `V5_RUNTIME_RESTART_SMOKE_OK`: crashes immediately after investigator, author, critic, quick, and
  discovery episode event boundaries resumed without repeating completed role/evaluator calls.
- `V5_RUNTIME_NOVELTY_TERMINAL_SMOKE_OK`: no-novel and novelty-exhausted made no author/critic calls,
  records, or checkpoint.
- `V5_RUNTIME_CRITIC_UNAVAILABLE_SMOKE_OK`: failed critic preserved typed authority and made no
  records/checkpoint.
- `V5_RUNTIME_CANCELLATION_SMOKE_OK`: pre-stage cancellation made zero role calls.

Final source verification used `py_compile`, Ruff check/format, package export import, forbidden
coupling scan, and `git diff --check`. No provider, Docker, replay, market data, or external process
was invoked.

## Final review correction

- Added a closed, indexed `CandidateStageResultPayloadV5` journal authority for validation,
  semantic-probe, quick-evaluation, and discovery-evaluation results. Typed stage failures are
  create-only artifacts authenticated on append/load. Recovery now reuses each durable local result
  and refuses to invoke a missing earlier stage once a later result or failure exists.
- Reconstructed every expected final `ExperimentRecordV5` inside the controller from the complete
  `CandidateEvidenceV5` value and the matching critic review/reference. The injected record factory
  output must equal that exact tuple; a structurally valid substituted review was rejected before
  persistence.
- Added a typed durable `runtime_failed` round outcome. Primary terminal authority is appended before
  cleanup; incomplete cleanup is the sole permitted post-terminal retry path, and its failure is
  reported separately without replacing the primary failure.
- Checkpoint publication now validates the requested generation/reference set and records the returned
  checkpoint before the post-call deadline check. Validation and cleanup also have controller-side
  post-call deadline checks, and runtime construction is inside the sanitizing entry boundary.

The final bounded direct fakes additionally produced:

- `RESTART_AFTER_CRITIC_ZERO_DUPLICATE_OK`: after durable critic completion and a restart before
  checkpoint, validation/probe/quick/four-episode/role counters remained unchanged and the canonical
  critic request identity was identical.
- `RECORD_SUBSTITUTION_REJECTED_OK`: a valid-looking record with substituted critic content failed as
  `finalization/invalid_dependency_result`.
- `CLEANUP_FAILURE_RETRY_PRESERVES_PRIMARY_OK`: terminal failure preceded cleanup, incomplete cleanup
  retried to completion, and primary failure authority remained unchanged.
- `CHECKPOINT_GENERATION_AND_POST_COMMIT_DEADLINE_OK`: a wrong generation failed closed; a valid
  committed checkpoint remained recorded when its post-call deadline fired.
- `CONSTRUCTOR_EXCEPTION_SANITIZED_OK`: an exception from the initial clock returned stable
  `recovery/stage_failed` without exposing its message.

## Post-commit authority correction

An exact valid `publish_projection` result is now the irreversible round-commit authority. The
runtime canonicalizes and records the current-round record refs and checkpoint without a post-commit
round-deadline abort. Any later exception is routed through completed cleanup handling and cannot
append `runtime_failed` or return the checkpoint as absent.

Recovery authenticates/reduces the projection first. An exact advanced state must bind the current
round's finalized records, the complete ordered checkpoint ref set, and a generation equal to the
number of finalized record-bearing rounds. That checkpoint is adopted before journal terminal
interpretation. This deliberately lets an authenticated advanced checkpoint outrank the stale
post-checkpoint `runtime_failed` shape produced by the immediately preceding implementation, while
still scheduling only owned cleanup and no role or candidate work.

The focused direct fake produced `POST_COMMIT_CHECKPOINT_PRECEDENCE_OK`: publication completed as the
round clock expired; both the first result and restart reported the same checkpoint and current-round
refs, no runtime-failure event was appended, an injected contradictory legacy terminal was ignored,
cleanup was not duplicated, and all role/validator/prober/quick/discovery counters stayed zero.
